                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A simple, minimalist physics puzzle game that’s easy to pick up and hard to put down. The basic idea is to keep a block balanced on a platform long enough to pass the level, and each stage changes things up just enough to make you stop and think. The presentation is clean and low-key, with no story and no fuss, so you can just play a few levels and go. It’s short, the visuals are very basic, and some levels can feel trial-and-error, so it’s not for anyone who wants depth. But for a chill, cheap little puzzler to play in short bursts, it’s a good time, and the reviews on Steam are very positive. Achievement farmer.",
